# docket configuration — copy to `.env` and edit (every field is
# DK_-prefixed and env-overridable). Code defaults are the SAFE, backend-generic
# choice: they assume a stock llama-server chat backend with NO embeddings, so
# retrieval degrades to sparse-only rather than erroring. Uncomment a block below
# to opt into a richer backend.

# --- Backend (OpenAI-/v1) ---------------------------------------------------
# DK_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# DK_CHAT_MODEL=gemma4:e2b        # e2b keeps chat + embed + OCR inside 6 GB VRAM

# --- All-in-one server ------------------------------------------------------
# A backend serving chat + embeddings (+ OCR at /v1/ocr) on one /v1 base lets you
# point DK_EMBED_URL at the SAME URL to turn dense hybrid retrieval on.
# Per-token logprobs on /v1/chat/completions power the trust/reliability labels.
# DK_EMBED_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# DK_EMBED_MODEL=embed-gemma:latest

# --- Cross-encoder reranker (T26, the dominant FinanceBench lever) -----------
# An all-in-one server also serves /v1/rerank (Cohere shape). Point the rerank
# endpoint at the same /v1 base to reorder fused candidates with a cross-encoder;
# unset => the fused RRF order stands (offline-safe). The seam uses rank order
# only, so any served reranker fits (qwen3-reranker-0.6b | bge-reranker-v2-m3).
# DK_RERANK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# DK_RERANK_MODEL=qwen3-reranker-0.6b:latest   # Phase-A sweep winner

# --- Dedicated embedding endpoint (stock llama-server) ----------------------
# Or run a separate `llama-server --embeddings` (e.g. EmbeddingGemma-300m) on
# another port and point DK_EMBED_URL there — do NOT add --embeddings to the
# shared chat server.
# DK_EMBED_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11435/v1

# --- Free-tier API providers ------------------------------------------------
# DK_PROVIDER=cerebras            # or: groq
# DK_CEREBRAS_API_KEY=...
# DK_GROQ_API_KEY=...
